              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "**Gauge guide**\n\nChemistry and flow colors match the ranges WaterGuru supplies for this pool. Labels show its preferred targets; green spans its acceptable band.\n\n| Reading | Target | Green range |\n|---|---|---|\n| Salt | ~3,200 ppm | 3,000–3,500 ppm |\n| Free chlorine | 3 ppm | 1.6–5.4 ppm |\n| pH | 7.6 | 7.5–7.7 |\n| Alkalinity | 80 ppm | 50–130 ppm |\n| Stabilizer (CYA) | 65 ppm | 30–100 ppm |\n| Calcium hardness | 400 ppm | 300–500 ppm |\n| Skimmer flow | 15 gal/min | 5–79 gal/min |\n\nWaterGuru account ranges captured October 3, 2026; these gauge bands are a saved snapshot, not automatically updated. [WaterGuru saltwater targets](https://support.waterguru.com/hc/en-us/articles/52236844676635-Why-does-WaterGuru-recommend-a-Calcium-Hardness-level-of-400-ppm-for-my-Saltwater-chlorine-generator-pool) support pH 7.6 and calcium 400 ppm. CYA targets depend on pool conditions.\n\nSalt uses [Jandy section 4.7](https://www.jandy.com/-/media/zodiac/global/downloads/jandy/water-sanitizers/h0325600.pdf); its yellow/red margins remain dashboard attention bands. Temperature stays neutral blue. Colors are not dosing instructions or swimming-safety certification; consider CYA, sample age, and WaterGuru advice."
